        "title": "The Constant Multiple Rule",
        "text": "Dividing by $$3$$ is the same as multiplying by $$\\frac{1}{3}$$. If $$f(x)=c g{\\left(x\\right)}$$, then $$f'(x)=c \\operatorname{g'}\\left(x\\right)$$, so you can take the derivative of the numerator and then divide by $$3$$.",
